Bless me father, for I have sinned. My last ascension was 2 years, 5
months ago. :P

I just achieved my second ascension. I was beginning to wonder if it
was ever going to happen. Granted, I haven't played nearly as much
since my first, and I've spread my time out across multiple roles.

I'll just hit the highlights:

There was a BoH and a magic lamp in minetown. I stole/credit cloned
for protection money. Got a luckstone and a touchstone from the bottom
of the mines. My pet killed the mine town priest before I was done
with the protection racket, but I was able to find another one for
naked AC -1.

Sac-festing got me Cleaver, then Stormbringer, then a bunch of junk
artifacts. Sokoban had an amulet of reflection, and I rounded things
out with a wish for GDSM from the magic lamp. The quest went smoothly
except that my pet (then a stone golem) was killed on the bottom
level, presumably by a troll. Efforts to revive him were unsuccessful.

More saccing summoned Juiblex and Yeenoghu (oops!), but thankfully I
was chaotic. Eventually I got Fire Brand, and somehow got crowned. I
didn't get jack squat for it, though, since I already had Stormbringer
and practically every resistance.

I wasn't paying attention on Medusa's Island and accidentally put a
wand of cancellation in my BoH. That was very frustrating, but I had
back-ups of all my essential equipment. I still hate that, though.
Around this time, I also managed to pray too soon after making a wish,
and lost all my protection. These were the two big mistakes of the
game. Ft. Ludios didn't exist in my game, so I had to kill the only
other priest outside of Gehennom just to get enough of my money back
to pull off the protection racket a second time. Losing protection at
XL23 is very painful. I never did get back down to naked -1AC, but I
eventually got to 1AC.

I didn't find a scroll of genocide until the plane of Earth, so
Gehennom was a bit more challenging than usual.

Of the demon princes, Juiblex was the first to die, though not in his
own habitat. I killed Asmodeus, who summoned Dispater. Both of them
went down easily. I was amused by Asmodeus, though. I initially fell
past his level through a trap door and entered from below. I saw that
he was peaceful, and just skirted around him to attack another demon
in the room. I had forgotten about being able to pay him off. So I was
a little surprised and amused when I saw:

"The invisible Asmodeus whispers at thin air. Asmodeus gets angry!"

Then he zapped a wand of fire directly at a wall and hit himself with
the ricochet. Oh, those wacky demon princes!

Orcus town contained Frost Brand in an abandoned shop. I later ID-ed
it and found it was cursed and -2. I didn't realize that was possible
before now. Orcus started the fight by quaffing a cursed potion of
gain level, which I also found hilarious. It also made things a lot
easier. I went up one level and immediately teleported to the up
stairs. He went down in about 3 turns, wasting only one charge of his
wand of death.

Just to be stylish and oh-so-original, I beat Vlad to death with a
magic flute. I think he hit me once.

After clearing out the rest of Gehennom and marking out the vibrating
square, I realized that I probably wasn't going to find any more
candles (and I didn't), so I used a wish for a few more. I left
Gehennom to take care of last minute business at my stash and prepare
for the ascension run.

The rest of the game went pretty smoothly. I got the book, did the
Invocation, and nabbed the amulet. The mysterious force hassled me a
little, but it could have been worse. I killed the Wizard a few times,
but he didn't give me much trouble, either. I never used the wands of
death I collected. Eventually they got blown up on the plane of Water
thanks to your friendly neighborhood electric eel. The Plane of Earth
and Air were pretty easy, as was the Plane of Fire. I had a few run-
ins with Archons, but nothing I couldn't handle. The Plane of Water
was a little nerve-wracking. On my last ascension, I had blessed
genocided all ;. I was really unsettled at the possibility of getting
drowned at this point in the game, but I luckily never had to deal
with it.

I actually found Demonbane on a fire giant in the plane of Water. It's
about the weirdest place I can think of to find an artifact.

The Astral plane wasn't too much to deal with. I ran to the wrong
altar first, killing Death a few times getting in and out. I brought a
long quite a few wands of teleportation, but never actually used them.
I made my way to the second altar (this time the center), killing
Famine before he ever got a hit. This was the right altar, so I never
killed Pestilence.

The Blessed +6 Fire Brand #two-weaponed with a blessed +6 silver saber
were my weapons of choice. My final AC was -38 while two-weaponing, or
-40 with a shield of reflection. I never used an amulet of life
saving, but ascended with two of them.



